00:05:31,764 --> 00:05:37,764
Because everyone loves an accurate period piece.

2
00:11:03,529 --> 00:11:09,529
A Cock and Bull Story is a comedy, history film
directed by Michael Winterbottom.

3
00:16:35,294 --> 00:16:41,294
Steve Coogan, an arrogant actor with low self-esteem and a complicated love life, is playing the eponymous role in an
adaptation of "The Life and Opinions of Tristram Shandy, Gentleman" being filmed at a stately home.

4
00:22:07,058 --> 00:22:13,058
He constantly spars with actor Rob Brydon, who is playing Uncle Toby and
believes his role to be of equal importance to Coogan's.

5
00:27:38,823 --> 00:27:44,823
Tristram Shandy / Walter Shandy / Steve Coogan, played by Steve Coogan.

6
00:33:10,588 --> 00:33:16,588
Toby Shandy / Rob Brydon, played by Rob Brydon.

7
00:38:42,352 --> 00:38:48,352
Elizabeth Shandy / Keeley Hawes, played by Keeley Hawes.

8
00:44:14,117 --> 00:44:20,117
Susannah / Shirley Henderson, played by Shirley Henderson.

9
00:49:45,882 --> 00:49:51,882
Trim, played by Raymond Waring.

10
00:55:17,647 --> 00:55:23,647
Six-Year-Old Tristam, played by Conal Murphy.

11
01:00:49,411 --> 01:00:55,411
A Cock and Bull Story (marketed in Australia, New Zealand and the United States as Tristram Shandy: A Cock and Bull
Story, and also credited as such) is a 2005 British comedy film directed by Michael Winterbottom.

12
01:06:21,176 --> 01:06:27,176
It is a film-within-a-film, featuring Steve Coogan and Rob Brydon playing themselves as egotistical actors during the
making of a screen adaptation of Laurence Sterne's 18th-century metafictional novel Tristram Shandy.

13
01:11:52,941 --> 01:11:58,941
Gillian Anderson and Keeley Hawes also play themselves in
addition to their Tristram Shandy roles.

14
01:17:24,705 --> 01:17:30,705
Since the book is about a man attempting but failing to write his autobiography,
the film takes the form of being about failing to make the film.

15
01:22:56,470 --> 01:23:02,470
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, film in film, filmmaking.

16
01:28:28,235 --> 01:28:34,235
The tone is lighthearted.
